                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1409: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-15T18:00:00-05:00">March 15, 1933—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. Your 140, March 7, 1 p.m. and 148, March 13, 8 p.m. If and when Council
                    invites the United States to collaborate with the Advisory Committee set up to
                    watch the Leticia situation, you may reply in the same terms as the note quoted
                    in Department’s 86 of March 11, 8 p.m.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d533-f1"/>
                    regarding the Far Eastern situation. You will also be guided in your action by
                    paragraph 2 of that instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
